 "supervisor_summary": "Netflix beat Q3 but cut the 2026 ad outlook to ~$2.7B and FCF to ~$12.0B and guided Q4 below the street. The stock is $64.89 after hours (17.1x FY27 EPS), below its 52-week low. After revision all five forecasters sit at 18x NTM P/E and fair values of $72.4-74.3; I re-derived the multiple and peer median (20.4x on one basis after the citation gate) myself rather than relying on that convergence. The one new fact I settled is that Paramount-WBD closed on 2026-10-06 (WBD 8-K), which three agents still treated as pending. Its modest margin effect gives a reconciled fair value of $72.74 (bear $49.25 / bull $91.65), within 1% of the mean. The ladder therefore stays at the mean (P(>= $69) 0.49), with the thesis break at $48 and the January FY27 guide as the next test.",
